meta {
  name: Video - Generate
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/v1/videos/generations
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{api_key}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "model": "google/veo-2",
    "prompt": "A time-lapse of clouds moving over a mountain range at golden hour",
    "duration": 5,
    "aspect_ratio": "16:9",
    "resolution": "1080p"
  }
}

docs {
  # Video Generation API

  Generate videos using Google Veo 2 and Veo 3 models.

  ## Endpoint
  `POST /v1/videos/generations`

  ## Authentication
  Required. Use Bearer token authentication with your API key.

  ## Request Body

  ### Required Parameters
  - `model` (string) - Model ID to use:
    - `google/veo-2` - Veo 2 (5-8 second videos)
    - `google/veo-3` - Veo 3 (up to 10 seconds, advanced features)
  - `prompt` (string) - Text description of the video (max 4000 characters)

  ### Optional Parameters
  - `duration` (integer) - Video duration in seconds (1-10). Default: 5
  - `aspect_ratio` (string) - Video aspect ratio: "16:9" or "9:16". Default: "16:9"
  - `resolution` (string) - Video resolution: "720p" or "1080p". Default: "1080p"
  - `fps` (integer) - Frames per second (12-60). Default: 24
  - `person_generation` (string) - Person generation policy:
    - "allow_all" (default) - Allow all person generation
    - "allow_adult" - Only allow adult person generation
    - "dont_allow" - Don't generate people
  - `seed` (integer) - Random seed for reproducibility
  - `negative_prompt` (string) - What to avoid in the generation
  - `image` (object | array) - Reference image(s) for image-to-video:
    - Single image: `{"data": "base64...", "type": "image/png"}`
    - Multiple images: Array of image objects
  - `response_format` (string) - "url" (default) or "b64_json"

  ## Response

  Returns a task ID for async processing (video generation takes 5+ minutes):
  ```json
  {
    "taskId": "xyz789",
    "status": "pending",
    "type": "video",
    "createdAt": 1234567890,
    "message": "Video generation task created. Use GET /v1/tasks/:taskId to check status."
  }
  ```

  Poll the task status using `GET /v1/tasks/{taskId}` until complete.

  ## Model Comparison

  | Feature | Veo 2 | Veo 3 |
  |---------|-------|-------|
  | Max Duration | 8 seconds | 10 seconds |
  | Quality | High | Ultra High |
  | Speed | ~5 min | ~8 min |
  | Advanced Features | ❌ | ✅ (better physics, lighting) |

  ## Examples

  ### Basic Text-to-Video
  ```json
  {
    "model": "google/veo-2",
    "prompt": "A cat playing with yarn in slow motion",
    "duration": 5,
    "aspect_ratio": "16:9",
    "resolution": "1080p"
  }
  ```

  ### Image-to-Video
  ```json
  {
    "model": "google/veo-3",
    "prompt": "Animate this image with flowing water and moving clouds",
    "image": {
      "data": "base64_encoded_image",
      "type": "image/png"
    },
    "duration": 8,
    "aspect_ratio": "16:9"
  }
  ```

  ### Advanced Settings
  ```json
  {
    "model": "google/veo-3",
    "prompt": "Cinematic shot of a spaceship landing on an alien planet",
    "duration": 10,
    "aspect_ratio": "16:9",
    "resolution": "1080p",
    "fps": 30,
    "person_generation": "dont_allow",
    "negative_prompt": "blurry, low quality, distorted",
    "seed": 12345
  }
  ```

  ## Processing Time
  - Veo 2: ~5-6 minutes per video
  - Veo 3: ~8-10 minutes per video
  - All video requests are async-only due to long processing times

  ## Error Responses

  ### 400 Bad Request
  - Invalid model ID
  - Invalid duration (must be 1-10 seconds)
  - Invalid aspect ratio
  - Invalid resolution

  ### 401 Unauthorized
  - Missing or invalid API key

  ### 402 Payment Required
  - Insufficient credits

  ## Pricing
  - Veo 2: ~$0.10 per second
  - Veo 3: ~$0.15 per second
  - Calculated based on actual video duration generated
}
